    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **66 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag on owner creation. When an owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), the created owner now reports `capacityWarning = true`. The existing hard rejection at 50 is untouched.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` flag.\n\n2. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `capacity_warning` column so the flag persists (and is read back by `GET /api/owners/{id}`).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean property to the `OwnerDto` schema, so the generated DTO carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically (same field name \u2192 auto-mapped).\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, set `owner.setCapacityWarning(isCityApproachingCapacity(owner.getCity()))`, and added the `isCityApproachingCapacity` helper: it counts existing owners in the city (case-insensitive, before persist, matching the existing capacity rule) and returns `true` when the count is in `[40, 50)`.\n\nThe count is taken after the hard-limit rejection, so it reflects the pre-persist city population; a city at 40\u201349 yields the warning, and the rejection at 50 remains unchanged.",
